  "gaps": [
    "The live R&D page publishes counts but no clear snapshot date; figures are reproduced as displayed, not calculated from selected items. Its registration count differs from the later asset-specific filings; do not treat it as a reconciled November total.",
    "TQB3909 registration and internal discovery are stated in the August company update; its disease list is supported by the R&D page. The specific filed indication was not verified.",
    "Bepirovirsen is an antisense oligonucleotide, represented as modality other because the allowed modality list lacks ASO. Its exact development code was not verified.",
    "Origins remain unverified for M701 and tecotabart vedotin. Lanifibranor’s licence is established by a September 2022 source, older than June 2026. Bepirovirsen is a mainland-China commercial partnership with GSK, represented as licensed.",
    "TQB2102 Phase 3 breast-cancer data were presented at ESMO on October 23, 2026; this completed event is not a next milestone. No future milestone was verified for the nine selected assets besides bepirovirsen.",
    "Bepirovirsen is approved in Japan and the US; the retained registration entry refers specifically to the pending mainland-China application and CTTQ commercial rights."
  ]
